                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "128a67b9-7a7b-4a90-9b47-8f540531db35",
                                "sense_id": "321c582e-954d-35c5-a26c-49bdf95645f3",
                                "text": "A series of interrupted sutures of No. 1 catgut are now inserted into the fascia layer immediately below the vaginal epithelium. These encover the thread sutures and further reinforce the action of the thread \"sling\"."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a82175d-3f77-4d46-b981-7c44423382fe",
                                "sense_id": "321c582e-954d-35c5-a26c-49bdf95645f3",
                                "text": "The difference between the two is that the Kānvas conclude with only the statement that by ācamana, the prāṇa itself is encovered or enclothed, while the Mādhyandinas further add the injuction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47e340eb-3eb5-41ba-963b-6c4a1ae47a3d",
                                "sense_id": "321c582e-954d-35c5-a26c-49bdf95645f3",
                                "text": "The theme can be expressed in an architectural analogy. For, of all contriving to encover space, the arch — alone or 'circulared' into the dome — is the most ingenious."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5b96755-baa8-4c77-9a15-529f5e073036",
                                "sense_id": "321c582e-954d-35c5-a26c-49bdf95645f3",
                                "text": "Finally, awareness of context and of what concepts can signify or encover in relation to it, requires that we critically examine ..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
